现有公开资料显示：Multiple Chinese embodied intelligence companies focus on a 'robot brain' technical route, developing large foundational models  
for robots as their core technology stack.；Digua Robot pursues a core-components-and-infrastructure technical path that combines custom robot     
chips with a dedicated robot operating system.；Guanglun Intelligent builds its technical path around physics simulation engines and synthetic data
generation to support embodied AI training.；Magic Atom adopts a '1+2+N' platform strategy in embodied robotics, using two core hardware platforms 
(MagicBot humanoid and MagicDog quadruped) plus a unified intelligent base to enable cross‑scenario data sharing and algorithm reuse.。[9]         

现有公开资料显示：Figure AI integrates OpenAI’s ChatGPT large language model into its humanoid robot Figure 01 so that natural language commands   
can be translated into embodied tasks like handing an apple, placing plates, or inserting coffee capsules while correcting position                
errors.；Tesla’s Optimus humanoid robot follows a factory‑operations technical route that combines humanoid manipulation with Tesla’s manufacturing
environment, as demonstrated by battery sorting tasks on the production line.；Chinese humanoid robot makers such as UBTECH (Walker series),       
Unitree (Unitree R1) and Songyan Power (Bumi) pursue a cost‑reduction path via smaller consumer‑oriented humanoid designs, lowering single‑robot   
costs from the million‑RMB level to tens of thousands of RMB.；Chinese humanoid robot execution‑component suppliers follow a cost‑advantage        
hardware route where actuators (linear, rotary, dexterous hands) account for roughly 73% of humanoid key component value and Chinese manufacturing 
lowers actuator costs by about 30–40% compared with Europe and the US.。[9][8][11]                                                                 

现有公开资料显示：National–local co‑built embodied intelligence robot innovation centers in China, such as those in Shanghai and Beijing, adopt an 
open‑source ecosystem route by planning or launching the open sourcing of general humanoid reference designs (e.g., Qinglong) and the ‘Tiangong’   
robot’s mechanical drawings, software architecture, electrical system and datasets.。[9]                                                           

